3D Exporter

[] Vertex positions (with indices?)
[] Vertex color
[] Frame data (frame count?)
[] Per animation, per frame vertex data (positions for now)

This should generate a .3d file that can be something like:

```
object_name <value>
fps <value>
animation_count <value>

vertex-data
<value>
value here is:
(default vertex positions (vec3)
vertex colors (vec3))[]

animations
(animation_1(the name of the animation)
<value>
value here is:
frame_1
<value>
value here is:
vertex position for the frame (vec3)[])[]
```
